<title>MALAYSIA: Kuala Lumpur tin market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Kuala Lumpur tin market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kuala Lumpur tin market is closed on Wednesday for the Buddhist Wesak day observance. The market reopens on Thursday, May 22.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, Malaysia's tin price fell four cents to 14.13 ringgit ($5.65) a kg on selling prompted by an overnight loss on the London Metal Exchange (LME).</p>
<p>Turnover was up to 90 tonnes from 54 on Monday. The local premium over London narrowed to $65 from $80.</p>
